It's already Friday, October 23 in Australia and New Zealand, which means customers who pre-ordered an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> are beginning to receive their devices.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/boardiesboi-duo-australia.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1208" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072313" /><br/>
We are seeing <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-duo-is-here-first-impressions-and-photos-thread.2492438/">first impressions and early photos</a> from actual customers on the <em>MacRumors</em> forums, Instagram, Reddit, and other social networks. If your &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; has been delivered, let us know what you think of it in the comments below. <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-duo-is-here-first-impressions-and-photos-thread.2492438/"><em>MacRumors</em> reader Boardiesboi</a> is always one of the first to get a new iPhone and share images. <br/>
<br/>
Priced starting at &#36;1,999, the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is Apple's first foldable device, featuring a 5.4-inch outer display and a 7.6-inch inner display.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/boardiesboi-duo-australia-hello.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1511" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072314" /><br/>
Apple says retail stores in select countries will have a limited number of iPhone Duos for walk-in purchases on launch day, and it expects stock to sell out fast due to "extraordinary" demand. There is no <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-store/">Apple Store</a> in New Zealand, so store stock in Australia will give us an idea of what in-store availability might look like worldwide.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/boardiesboi-duo-australia-folded.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1529" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072315" /><br/>
Apple Stores in the United States, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Canada, Italy (select stores), Mexico, Macao (launch day only), Germany, the Netherlands, Singapore, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland, Türkiye, and the UK will have some iPhone Duos for walk-in customers.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; will not be available for walk-in purchase in France, China, Hong Kong, India, Japan, Malaysia, South Korea, Taiwan, Thailand, and the United Arab Emirates, so customers in those locations will need a reservation for &zwnj;Apple Store&zwnj; pickup.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's website advises customers to check back on Saturday, October 24 for pickup reservations. Shipping estimates for online orders slipped to January 25 shortly after pre-orders started and have stayed there since. Purchasing on launch day or getting lucky with a pickup reservation at a later date is the best chance of getting an &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; this year.<br/>
<br/>
It's possible some carriers and big-box stores could also have stock available on launch day.<br/>
<br/>
